  "abstract": "Building on the SOTA MoFL architecture (ID 285), this experiment tests a refined gating mechanism. Instead of the spatial CNN gater operating on the raw, high-dimensional input, this model uses a simple MLP gater that operates directly on the compressed latent representation (`factors_in`). The hypothesis is that gating on the latent factors provides a more direct and informative signal for selecting the appropriate expert factor loadings, leading to improved performance and a more robust model.",
  "submitted_tick": 153,
